#====================================================================
# E321 draft - Test-only bootstrap download blocks an offline package build
#====================================================================

id:                     E321
trigger_tool:           cmake|conan|FetchContent|ExternalProject
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        Each download failed.*googletest|google/googletest/archive.*failed|Performing download step.*googletest|BUILD_TESTING.*GoogleTest

severity:               2
category:               build-system|cmake|conan|testing|network
match_keywords:         BUILD_TESTING, GoogleTest, googletest, FetchContent, ExternalProject, configure-time download, offline CI, Conan test_package
title:                  Separate test-only bootstrap downloads from an offline package build

root_cause:             Some CMake projects fetch a test framework during configure as soon as BUILD_TESTING is enabled. The production library has no such runtime requirement, but an offline or rate-limited CI worker cannot even configure the package while the test-only bootstrap is active.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for CMake projects whose upstream test option triggers FetchContent or ExternalProject downloads, when the build worker cannot reliably fetch or cache the test framework.
verification_cmd:       cmake -DBUILD_TESTING=ON <source> 2>&1 | grep -Ei 'googletest|FetchContent|ExternalProject|Downloading'; conan create .; conan test test_package <reference>

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           disable-networked-upstream-tests-and-run-consumer-test
rec_description:        Keep the package build deterministic by setting BUILD_TESTING=OFF when enabling it performs a network bootstrap. Retain an executable Conan test_package that links the installed target and exercises representative public API behavior. Record any host-side upstream-suite result separately and do not transfer it to the target CI result.
rec_command:            CMakeToolchain(self).variables['BUILD_TESTING'] = 'OFF'; conan create .; conan test test_package <reference>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-and-consumer-test

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      supply-a-pinned-offline-test-dependency
fallback_description:   If full upstream CTest coverage is required, vendor or inject the exact checked test-framework source through a repository-approved, checksummed offline dependency path, then execute and report that suite separately from production package creation.
fallback_command:       cmake -DBUILD_TESTING=ON -DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_GOOGLETEST=<checked-source> <source>; ctest --output-on-failure
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          approved-offline-dependency

forbid_1_pattern:       BUILD_TESTING=ON.*(network|GitHub|googletest).*ignore|cmake.*\|\| true
forbid_1_reason:        Ignoring a configure-time test dependency failure leaves no configured package and hides an unreproducible network prerequisite.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI intermittently fails before compilation or publishes unverified build evidence.
forbid_2_pattern:       local.*56/56.*OHOS|OHOS.*56/56.*local
forbid_2_reason:        A host-side upstream CTest result and a target-side consumer test exercise different environments and must be reported independently.
forbid_2_consequence:   The PR overstates target coverage and makes the test record non-auditable.
forbid_3_pattern:       BUILD_TESTING=OFF.*no.*test_package|disable.*test.*without.*consumer
forbid_3_reason:        Disabling an upstream suite removes a validation layer; a real consumer test is the minimum replacement for package install and public linkage behavior.
forbid_3_consequence:   A package can compile but expose a broken CMake target, ABI, runtime dependency, or basic API path.

principles:             P002, P003, P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E017, E217, E221, E224]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

